{
  "title": "Web Settings breaks when the ingredient-name status request fails",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/pages/SettingsPage.tsx reads the ingredient-name status createResource with no error handling, and the app has no ErrorBoundary. \
In Solid, reading a resource that errored throws, so one failed /api/ingredient-names/status request most likely takes down the Settings page; the same read feeds failedCount() and the 2 s poll effect. \
Fix: handle the resource's error state (show the section as unavailable, keep polling with backoff). \
Separately, decide whether this section belongs in end-user Settings at all: it shows internal states (reasking, reask_failed) and raw LLM error strings, and iOS has no counterpart. \
If it stays, it needs an iOS version (AGENTS.md: both clients by default); if it's an operator tool, move it out of user Settings. \
The calorie architecture issue (p2-calorie-architecture) may remove most of these states anyway.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "web",
    "ios",
  ],
